    "q-183517": {
      "dom_id": "step-q183517",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$\\,$ $K(y):$ $y$ is prime\n\nGiven the predicate above, which of the following expresses the statement $∃y\\in Q,\\,K(y)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The existential quantifier \"$∃$\" means \"there exists.\" So, the statement \n$∃y\\in Q,\\,K(y)$ \nreads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **There exists** $y\\in Q$ **such that** $y$ is prime.\n\n**Note:** This statement is true.",
